   Scavenger — Misuse of Error-Handling Code → QEMU/KVM Escape
   (Black Hat Asia 2021 / CVE-2020-25084)

   Affected:  QEMU 5.x  (hw/block/nvme.c + dma-helpers.c)
   Bug:       nvme_dma_read_prp() / nvme_dma_write_prp() pass a
              stack-allocated QEMUSGList to nvme_map_prp(); on the
              error path, qemu_sglist_destroy() frees qsg->sg even
              though the list was never fully initialised, allowing
              heap layout control for a subsequent UAF chain.
   Chain:     NVMe UAF → virtio-gpu heap leak → QEMU base leak →
              timer callback hijack → system() RCE on host.

   Offsets in exp.c are build-specific — re-derive with:
     nm ./qemu-system-x86_64 | grep -E '(^| )(system|nvme_process_sq|cleanup)\b'

   Run:  /exp    to trigger the escape
